-- title:
--   Unipotent inertia at q for the Taylor–Wiles Hecke-ring representation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, and let $p$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, that is, a rank-two $k$-vector space with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)=\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ trivial on the fixer of some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and assume $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible, i.e. its base change to $\overline k$ has no invariant subspace other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, $N\neq 0$ an integer all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, and $r$ a nonzero prime not dividing $N$. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from $\mathbb T=\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,N\,2\,S$, the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$) and $U_{q'}$ ($q'\mid N$, $q'\notin S$), and assume that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be pairwise distinct nonzero primes, none in $S$ and none equal to $r$, let $\pi_i\colon(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times\to\mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ be homomorphisms and $\alpha_i\in k$; write $L=N\bigl(\prod_i q_i\bigr)r$ and $H_Q=H_R\cap\ker\pi_Q\le(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$. Assume the two commutation hypotheses `OpComm` and `DiaComm` for the Hecke operators and the diamond operators on the cohomological carrier at level $L$ and subgroup $H_Q$, and let $T_Q=\mathrm{HeckeRing}$ be the resulting $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of the endomorphisms of the localised module, cut out by $\theta$ and $\alpha$. Assume $T_Q$ is local, Noetherian and complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, that $\mathcal O\to T_Q$ is a local homomorphism and makes $T_Q$ a finite $\mathcal O$-module, and that $\mathcal O\to T_Q\to T_Q/\mathfrak m_{T_Q}$ is surjective. Let $\rho'$ be an adically continuous Galois representation on a free $T_Q$-module of rank two such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid L$, every $P$ over $\ell$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$ for $P$ one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\rho'(\sigma)=T_\ell\in T_Q$, and such that the residual representation of $\rho'$ is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Finally let $q$ be a prime with $q\neq p$, $q\mid N$, $q^2\nmid L$, and suppose $\bar\rho$ is not unramified at $q$ (some inertia element at some place over $q$ acts nontrivially). Then $\rho'$ is unipotent on inertia at $q$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ having $q$ as a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho'(\sigma)$ equals $(X-1)^2$.
--
--   This is the local condition at a prime $q\neq p$ of type (A) in Wiles's deformation problem: the Galois representation carried by the Taylor–Wiles-level Hecke ring has unipotent image on inertia at a prime exactly dividing the level at which the residual representation is ramified. It is one of the local properties recorded when constructing the two-dimensional representation over the Hecke ring, and is used by [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_flat`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_flat) and [`CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary`](thm.html#CuspForm.TWLevel.exists_galoisRepAdic_moduleEnd_ML_of_not_isFlatAt_strictOrdinary).
